# Firebase service-account private key (FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS in .env).
# This is the SERVER credential — a different file from the Android client's
# App/android/app/google-services.json. It contains a private_key granting
# full Firebase Admin access to the project, so it must never be committed,
# and must never be placed anywhere under App/android/ (that tree is the
# Android project and can end up inside a distributable APK).
